WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.869
Earlier this week I was forced to share a cab

2
00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:03.786
to the Apollo Theater

3
00:00:03.786 --> 00:00:06.624
with our associate producer, Jordan Schlansky.

4
00:00:06.624 --> 00:00:09.457
(audience cheers)

5
00:00:14.726 --> 00:00:16.439
If you're at all familiar with Jordan,

6
00:00:16.439 --> 00:00:19.968
you know how painful an experience that was for me.

7
00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.433
Thankfully, I had my phone and one of our sponsors,

8
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:26.250
Google Play, to help me endure this session.

9
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.250
Take a look.

10
00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:31.593
Apollo Theater, please.

11
00:00:31.593 --> 00:00:34.801
Broadway was originally named by the Dutch

12
00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.309
in a colony of New Amsterdam.

13
00:00:37.309 --> 00:00:38.859
New Amsterdam.

14
00:00:38.859 --> 00:00:41.473
(Speaks in foreign language), or away,

15
00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:44.146
was a naturally created path,

16
00:00:44.146 --> 00:00:47.798
usually from heavy foot traffic or perhaps animals.

17
00:00:47.798 --> 00:00:50.636
Why are we riding together?

18
00:00:50.636 --> 00:00:51.719
How did this?

19
00:00:52.648 --> 00:00:54.667
We're both going in the same direction.

20
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:55.500
Shouldn't we, I know.

21
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:56.859
Why wouldn't we ride together.

22
00:00:56.859 --> 00:01:00.431
Well, do you really want me to answer that question?

23
00:01:00.431 --> 00:01:02.935
We wouldn't ride together

24
00:01:02.935 --> 00:01:05.668
because you're such an irritating person.

25
00:01:05.668 --> 00:01:06.792
(audience laughs)

26
00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:08.622
Do you mind if I open Google Play?

27
00:01:08.622 --> 00:01:12.245
Do something other than listen to you.

28
00:01:12.245 --> 00:01:14.955
I might play Angry Birds Match.

29
00:01:14.955 --> 00:01:16.402
Right.

30
00:01:16.402 --> 00:01:19.522
The Broadway that was present in New Amsterdam

31
00:01:19.522 --> 00:01:23.262
only went as high as (speaks in foreign language).

32
00:01:23.262 --> 00:01:26.159
Which is typically called Wall Street and, in fact,

33
00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:27.935
the reason it was called (speaks in foreign language).

34
00:01:27.935 --> 00:01:29.102
Ah, come on!

35
00:01:30.442 --> 00:01:32.419
Is because--
It's my fault.

36
00:01:32.419 --> 00:01:34.391
A wooden wall was present there

37
00:01:34.391 --> 00:01:38.332
to keep out anyone north of that point.

38
00:01:38.332 --> 00:01:41.497
I'm playing Angry Birds Match, I'm not looking at you,

39
00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:44.164
I'm totally engaged in this game,

40
00:01:44.164 --> 00:01:47.910
that's a signal to most people to maybe stop talking.

41
00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:50.989
Steam is a utility supplied by Con Edison.

42
00:01:50.989 --> 00:01:53.860
New York City has one of the highest quality

43
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.499
tap waters in the world.

44
00:01:55.499 --> 00:01:57.555
The maximum theoretical temperature

45
00:01:57.555 --> 00:01:59.984
of 212 degrees fahrenheit.

46
00:01:59.984 --> 00:02:02.488
The American version of Focaccia

47
00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.866
is a very dense, spongy bread.

48
00:02:04.866 --> 00:02:07.433
Duran Duran had a quote in their song, Steam in the Subway,

49
00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:10.386
which is technically incorrect.

50
00:02:10.386 --> 00:02:12.486
I consider the soundtrack to Footloose

51
00:02:12.486 --> 00:02:16.144
to be a bit overrated, I like the deep cuts.

52
00:02:16.144 --> 00:02:19.107
How many friends do you have, I mean real friends?

53
00:02:19.107 --> 00:02:20.749
Not concerned with friends.

54
00:02:20.749 --> 00:02:22.474
That means no friends.

55
00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:25.385
Jordan, it appears we are at the Apollo Theater.

56
00:02:25.385 --> 00:02:26.218
Yes.

57
00:02:26.218 --> 00:02:29.135
And I hope I never see you again.

58
00:02:33.169 --> 00:02:36.062
Now the marquee above us was originally, of course,

59
00:02:36.062 --> 00:02:37.826
an analog marquee, and--

60
00:02:37.826 --> 00:02:38.659
Got one.

61
00:02:40.953 --> 00:02:42.843
Now of course it's electronic, but can also--

62
00:02:42.843 --> 00:02:44.135
Can you stay here?
You stay here.

63
00:02:44.135 --> 00:02:44.968
Bye.

64
00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:47.175
(audience cheers)

65
00:02:47.175 --> 00:02:48.508
He's a real guy!

